From 3305e6ee11ace4fa71afc21196fa37baf43ff48e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:14:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 68/77] script: add OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S for SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s
 checks in P2MR leaves

Byte 0xf1, OP_SUCCESS241 in BIP 342, executes as OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S in a
P2MR leaf that is executed as tapscript (leaf version 0xc0, or 0xe0 with
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_TRIPWIRE, at depth one or more) when the new
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_SLHDSA128S flag is set. Then the pre-scan no longer
treats it as an OP_SUCCESSx; other OP_SUCCESSx bytes in the leaf still
are. Everywhere else the byte keeps its meaning: a bad opcode in legacy
and witness v0 scripts, and OP_SUCCESS241 in P2TR leaves and without the
flag. No deployment sets the flag yet.

The opcode takes the 32-byte public key (PK.seed || PK.root), pushed by
the leaf, and the 7856-byte signature in sixteen chunks: fifteen of 520
bytes, then 56, or 57 with an explicit hash type, so
MAX_SCRIPT_ELEMENT_SIZE does not change and every signature has one
encoding. The checks follow those of OP_CHECKMLDSA44, which follow
EvalChecksigTapscript, in the same ten steps: at least seventeen stack
elements; a signature with any non-empty chunk uses
VALIDATION_WEIGHT_PER_SLHDSA128S_CHECK units of validation weight; the
public key size; sixteen empty chunks push false; the chunk sizes; the
hash type, with the rules of BIP 341. The message is the BIP 341
signature message of a tapscript spend with key_version 2, so it never
equals that of a BIP 342 or an OP_CHECKMLDSA44 signature, and the check
is slh_verify of FIPS 205 (pure SLH-DSA, external interface) with the
context string "P2MR/SLHDSA128S/EXP0". An invalid signature fails the
script; a valid one pushes 1. Disabled elliptic curve checks in leaf
version 0xe0 do not touch it.

VALIDATION_WEIGHT_PER_SLHDSA128S_CHECK is 5000, final. The single-check
condition, C >= 1.25 x 50 x p99(worst-case SLH-DSA check) / median(Schnorr
check), measured over the whole path of a check on a machine without SHA
extensions, asked for 2550 to 3658; 5000 leaves a margin of at least
1.36x for weaker hardware. It stays below 8022, the budget of a
single-signature spend, so a single SLH1 spend and one check per
signature in any script fit. It never changes once a build carrying it
has left the network's own nodes.

- The checkers gain CheckSLHDSA128SSignature: the hash type and the
  message in GenericTransactionSignatureChecker, the verification in the
  virtual VerifySLHDSA128SSignature, which the caching checker overrides
  with cache entries under a fourth salted hasher, padded with 'H'.
  DeferringSignatureChecker passes the new check through.
- Four new script errors, SLHDSA128S_PUBKEY_SIZE, SLHDSA128S_SIG_SIZE,
  SLHDSA128S_SIG_HASHTYPE and SLHDSA128S_SIG, also in the error names of
  script_tests; OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S as an opcode name; the flag name
  P2MR_SLHDSA128S.
- The script_flags fuzz target leaves the new flag alone, as it does the
  other flags that turn an OP_SUCCESSx into an opcode.

See doc/p2mr-slhdsa128s.md, added later in this series.
